    "summary": "src/db/lance/conn.ts now connects with readConsistencyInterval 0, so a connection sees writes committed through another thread's connection. src/daemon/db/duckdb-pool.ts withConnection runs inside getStoreGuard().withStore('duckdb', ...) with a 10-minute permit wait, so each thread's in-memory instance is used one query at a time across the process (no withConnection call nests inside another). Found and fixed in src/db/store-guard.ts while testing: a pending Atomics.waitAsync does not keep a thread's event loop alive, so a thread whose only work was waiting for a permit exited silently; a timer now holds it for the length of the wait. Tests in src/db/__tests__/cross-thread-stores.test.ts use real workers; the existing duckdb-pool, duckdb-file-driver, duckdb-converted-driver, conn, artifact-vec, entity-vec and cleanup suites pass. Mutations (interval unset, guard bypassed, no keep-alive) each fail their target test.",
